---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { THEMATIC_DOMAINS } from '../lib/domains';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why the Algeria Earth Observatory exists, its scientific scope, independence, governance, open-data principles and long-term vision.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="About the Observatory" title="An open scientific initiative for Algeria’s environmental data" />
  <div class="container-aeo py-12 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_17rem] lg:gap-14">
    <div class="prose-aeo">
      <h2 id="mission">Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Algeria Earth Observatory is an open scientific initiative dedicated to making Earth observation and environmental information about Algeria
        accessible, discoverable, reusable, and scientifically documented. Through open data, interactive mapping, and collaborative research, the Observatory
        supports better understanding of Algeria’s agricultural landscapes, climate variability, land-use change, water resources, and environmental systems.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why">Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        A large and growing body of satellite and environmental data covers Algeria, but it is scattered across dozens of international portals, each with its own
        formats, account systems, licences and definitions. Researchers spend time rediscovering the same sources; important caveats — a cropland definition, a
        known processing error, a change of version — are easy to miss; and Algeria-specific derivatives are rarely documented well enough to be reused.
      </p>
      <p>The Observatory addresses this by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>documenting authentic datasets with their provenance, licence, resolution, period and limitations in one consistent format;</li>
        <li>stating clearly when a dataset is global and must be subset, and when it is held by the provider rather than by AEO;</li>
        <li>publishing Algeria-specific derivatives only with version, checksum and reproducible code;</li>
        <li>providing an interactive map for exploration, and guides for responsible use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="reproducibility">Reproducible Earth observation science</h2>
      <p>
        Results based on satellite products depend on product versions, definitions, processing choices and validation. AEO treats these as first-class information:
        every record distinguishes observed, derived and modeled data, discloses validation status, and links to the original source and citation.
        See <a href="/docs/quality-uncertainty/">Dataset quality and uncertainty</a> and <a href="/docs/reproducibility/">Geospatial reproducibility</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="scope">Scientific scope</h2>
      <p>The catalog is organised around six interconnected domains. Agriculture and cropland is the initial priority.</p>
      <ul>{THEMATIC_DOMAINS.map((d) => <li><a href={`/data/?domain=${d.id}`}>{d.title}</a> — {d.summary}</li>)}</ul>

      <h2 id="governance">Independence and governance</h2>
      <p>
        AEO is an independent initiative. It is <strong>not</strong> a government service, is not officially registered or nationally mandated, and is not
        affiliated with or endorsed by any institution. It is in its initial development phase and is exploring sustainable support models
        (see <a href="/support/">Support the Observatory</a>).
      </p>
      <p>The governance model is deliberately simple during the initial development phase:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>{SITE.founder ? <>The founding maintainer (<a href={`https://github.com/${SITE.founder.github}`} rel="noopener">{SITE.founder.name}</a>)</> : 'The founding maintainer'} sets overall project direction.</li>
        <li>Anyone can propose changes through GitHub issues and pull requests.</li>
        <li>Maintainers review scientific documentation, licence and sharing conditions, and technical compatibility before merging.</li>
        <li>Maintainers and scientific advisers are named publicly only after they have accepted the role.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The full text is in <a href={`${SITE.github.repoUrl}/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md`} rel="noopener">GOVERNANCE.md</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="principles">Open data principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Credit the source.</strong> Original producers keep the credit; their citation is shown first.</li>
        <li><strong>Respect licences.</strong> Data are only redistributed where the licence allows it; otherwise AEO links to the source.</li>
        <li><strong>No invented numbers.</strong> No fabricated accuracy figures, download counts, partnerships or statistics.</li>
        <li><strong>Transparency.</strong> Unverified information is marked as such; the <a href="/sources/">source audit</a> lists what was checked.</li>
        <li><strong>Separate licences.</strong> Website code (MIT) and text (CC BY 4.0) are licensed separately from each dataset.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="vision">Long-term vision</h2>
      <p>
        The ambition is a durable, community-maintained reference for Algerian environmental data — one that researchers in Algerian universities and
        laboratories, public institutions and international collaborators can rely on. Capabilities under consideration include wilaya- and watershed-level
        search and downloads, documented national cropland and drought products, reproducible notebooks, and DOI-based publication of AEO products.
        These are plans, not existing services; see the <a href={`${SITE.github.repoUrl}/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md`} rel="noopener">roadmap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="mt-12 lg:mt-0" aria-label="Summary">
      <div class="sticky top-24 space-y-4 rounded-md border border-line p-5 text-[0.9rem]">
        <p class="meta">At a glance</p>
        <dl class="space-y-3">
          <div><dt class="text-slate">Status</dt><dd class="text-graphite">{SITE.phase}</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="text-slate">Nature</dt><dd class="text-graphite">Independent, open, non-commercial initiative</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="text-slate">Support</dt><dd class="text-graphite">Exploring sustainable models — see <a href="/support/">Support</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt class="text-slate">Code</dt><dd class="text-graphite"><a href={SITE.github.repoUrl} rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
